  "passage": {
    "text": "Indirect costs can also be very high. They include delays to projects and lost working time. Damaged equipment is another factor. Companies also have to pay to find and train new workers to replace injured ones. On top of this, a poor safety record can damage a company's reputation. This may make it harder to win future contracts. It can also make it more difficult to attract new employees.",
